 ## Rendering
 
+- **Local EDR output experiment:** `DM_TGAA_EDR=1` requests an extended-linear-sRGB RGBA16Float Mac layer and decodes the existing scanout values using an explicit sRGB assumption. SDR white remains 1; output follows current screen headroom, with MetalFX disabled for this experiment. A 1080p/30 courtroom run on the built-in Retina display produced a same-present-shader offscreen peak of 1.256836; per-channel conversion error against the captured source stayed below 0.001. This verifies the output path, not measured panel luminance or a full color calibration. Installed apps remain unchanged; external-screen transitions and 4K/60 are untested.
+
+- **HDR exposure correction (Japanese local experiment):** the earlier scene-buffer maximum below 1 does not rule out recoverable highlights. `fp_c3` maps to cb reg0 `(0.5,2,1,1)`: material output is scaled by x=0.5, and postprocess `720e88a17ae787f6_b` multiplies by y=2 before clamping. Removing only its three RGB clamps in an isolated source override preserved a courtroom pre-UI peak of 1.11328125 across 19,048 pixels (0.9186%); the next copy and final game target retained the peak. `DM_TGAA_POSTPROCESS_SOURCE` runtime-compiles only this library when explicitly set; default uses the original metallib. This is shader-domain RGB evidence, not calibrated luminance or completed EDR display output. No installed application was changed.
+
+- **Local HDR measurement follow-up (Japanese 1.0.0):** opt-in `DM_NVN_TEXSNAP_MSAA=1` adds an independent same-format MSAA resolve at selected TEXSNAP pass ends, preserving the source samples with StoreAndMultisampleResolve. Five courtroom snapshots of the 2x RGBA16Float scene target peaked at 0.557129 before post-processing; no resolved pixel exceeded 1.0. This is an average resolve, not individual-sample inspection, and is not evidence that every scene lacks HDR data. Installed builds and EDR presentation are unchanged.
+
+- **Open local experiment, Japanese build only:** `DM_TGAA_FLOAT_PROBE=1` promotes GPU-only COMPRESSIBLE RGBA8 2D/MSAA targets to RGBA16Float. Default is off; packaged/CPU and linear textures remain unchanged. A Japanese 1.0.0, 1080p/30 courtroom capture ran with float targets and a matching SDR-off control. End-of-frame RGB peaked at 1.01367, only 0.0436% of pixels exceeded 1.001; this does not establish useful HDR lighting. Display output and shader clamps are unchanged. The local runner gates build `d871b992e95b71c541ddc834f63c664b` and uses copied test saves. International builds and other scenes were not tested.
+
 - Upper-left window origin, depth mode near = 0, a 1920x1080 RGBA8 swapchain; the game asks for present interval 1 and paces itself at 30 fps. Mario's binding layout (combined textures at `0x20 + 8 × slot`, slots 0–2).
 - **Resolved: black screen at boot, with the draws of a dialog box in the pass dump** (sampling 256x256 and 1024x256 textures of format 0x4d). No texture had been uploaded from guest memory (`packaged textures: first uploads 0`), and `DM_NVN_TEXINFO=1024x256` showed storage that already held data at first use (226,555 of 262,144 bytes non-zero): no packaged layout, block-linear, in a 1000 MB `CPU_CACHED | GPU_CACHED | COMPRESSIBLE` pool (flags 0xa4). A log of the pool flushes, texture creations and file reads (temporary lines under `DM_NVN_LOG`) showed how they are filled: every `.tex` is read into staging buffers (512 KB `ReadFile`s, none into the pool), and the CPU copies the texels into the texture's storage after `nvnTextureInitialize`, with no `nvnMemoryPoolFlushMappedRange` over them and no `WriteTexels`; only the four linear 1024x64 text textures are flushed, every frame. `main` has no cache maintenance instruction at all, so there is no flush for the host to take as the signal. With `tex_dirty_upload` a registered texture whose pages the CPU writes after creation is uploaded at its first use (as for FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles, [010038B015560000](../010038B015560000/README.md)).
+- **Resolved in the Japanese 1.0.0 build (`0100D7F00FB1A000`): missing title-room background.** Four 1024×1024 BC1 textures were filled before `nvnTextureInitialize`, so dirty-page tracking missed them: their guest memory held 475,029–515,634 non-zero bytes, but their Metal textures held only zeros. The [pre-registration content fix](../../../docs/reference/nvn-objects.md#cpu-texture-storage-filled-before-registration) uploads them on first use. The original Japanese game and the Chinese resource patch both showed the complete room in frame-600 Mac captures; the international build was not retested with this change.
 
 ## Services
 
