+
+## Mac input presentation
+
+### Connected controller still shows keyboard icons
+
+- **Symptom:** a preconnected controller works but the UI keeps keyboard prompts; choosing Switch can also retain prompts generated by the previous run.
+- **Cause:** the launcher snapshots GameController discovery before asynchronous connection delivery and loads a fixed archive overlay. The Switch branch previously left stale font overlays behind.
+- **Fix:** remove stale font overlays when selecting the original Switch atlas. For the opted-in Japanese TGAA launcher, generate immutable runtime atlas variants and let the host's actual connection/input events choose their style. Match the complete source texture bytes before substituting; invalidate sampled-view generations on changes. Manual presets remain fixed. Mouse movement and focus loss restore the cursor hidden by game-key/controller activity.
+- **Found on:** [The Great Ace Attorney Chronicles](../../dm/games/010036E00FB20000/README.md), local Japanese 1.0.0/CN1.3 Mac build. No fixed guest code addresses are involved.
+- **Check:** isolated courtroom captures of keyboard, Switch, Xbox and PlayStation, including transitions back; Pro Controller discovered by the actual host. Physical detach/reconnect and cursor behavior still need hands-on acceptance; other games are untested. Runtime atlas substitution is disabled without its explicit environment path and title gate.
